Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be even functions.
We want to determine if $f(x)g(x)$ is even, odd, or neither. 

Recall that a function $h(x)$ is even if $h(-x) = h(x)$ for all $x$, and odd if $h(-x) = -h(x)$ for all $x$. 

Let $h(x) = f(x)g(x)$. Then $h(-x) = f(-x)g(-x)$. 
Since $f(x)$ is even, $f(-x) = f(x)$. 
Since $g(x)$ is even, $g(-x) = g(x)$. 
Therefore, $h(-x) = f(x)g(x) = h(x)$. 
So $f(x)g(x)$ is an even function. 

